#: of pyvista.core.filters.data_set.DataSetFilters.extract_cells_by_type:10
msgid ""
"The type of output dataset is always the same as the input type. Since "
"structured types of data (i.e., :class:`pyvista.ImageData`, "
":class:`pyvista.StructuredGrid`, :class:`pyvista.RectilinearGrid`) are all "
"composed of a cell of the same type, the output is either empty, or a "
"shallow copy of the input. Unstructured data "
"(:class:`pyvista.UnstructuredGrid`, :class:`pyvista.PolyData`) input may "
"produce a subset of the input data (depending on the selected cell types)."
msgstr ""

