#: of pyvista.core.filters.image_data.ImageDataFilters.contour_labels:106
msgid ""
"Type of the output mesh. Can be either ``'quads'``, or ``'triangles'``. By "
"default, the output mesh has :attr:`~pyvista.CellType.TRIANGLE` cells when "
"``smoothing`` is enabled and :attr:`~pyvista.CellType.QUAD` cells (quads) "
"otherwise. The mesh type can be forced to be triangles or quads; however, if"
" smoothing is enabled and the type is ``'quads'``, the generated quads may "
"not be planar."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../../opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.13.14/x64/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pyvista/core/filters/image_data.pydocstring
#: of pyvista.core.filters.image_data.ImageDataFilters.contour_labels:114
msgid ""
"Name of scalars to process. Defaults to currently active scalars. If cell "
"scalars are specified, the input image is first re-meshed with "
":meth:`~pyvista.ImageDataFilters.cells_to_points` to transform the cell data"
" into point data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../../opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.13.14/x64/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pyvista/core/filters/image_data.pydocstring
#: of pyvista.core.filters.image_data.ImageDataFilters.contour_labels:119
msgid ""
"**orient_faces** : :ref:`bool <python:bltin-boolean-values>`, "
":obj:`optional`"
msgstr ""
"**orient_faces** : :ref:`bool <python:bltin-boolean-values>`, "
":obj:`optional`"

#: ../../../../../../../opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.13.14/x64/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pyvista/core/filters/image_data.pydocstring
#: of pyvista.core.filters.image_data.ImageDataFilters.contour_labels:122
msgid ""
"This keyword should not be used and will be removed in a future version. It "
"was meant to address a vtk bug where the faces generated by "
":vtk:`vtkSurfaceNets3D` have incorrect orientation. This bug is fixed in VTK"
" 9.6, and therefore the faces now always have correct orientation by "
"default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../../opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.13.14/x64/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pyvista/core/filters/image_data.pydocstring
#: of pyvista.core.filters.image_data.ImageDataFilters.contour_labels:127
msgid ""
"Orient the faces of the generated contours so that they have consistent "
"ordering and face outward. If ``False``, the generated polygons may have "
"inconsistent ordering and orientation, which can negatively impact "
"downstream calculations and the shading used for rendering."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../../opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.13.14/x64/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pyvista/core/filters/image_data.pydocstring
#: of pyvista.core.filters.image_data.ImageDataFilters.contour_labels:134
msgid ""
"Orienting the faces can be computationally expensive for large meshes. "
"Consider disabling this option to improve this filter's performance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../../opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.13.14/x64/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pyvista/core/filters/image_data.pydocstring
#: of pyvista.core.filters.image_data.ImageDataFilters.contour_labels:139
msgid ""
"Enabling this option is `likely` to generate surfaces with normals pointing "
"outward when ``pad_background`` is ``True`` and ``boundary_style`` is "
"``'external'`` (the default). However, this is not guaranteed if the "
"generated surface is not closed or if internal boundaries are generated. Do "
"not assume the normals will point outward in all cases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../../opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.13.14/x64/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pyvista/core/filters/image_data.pydocstring
#: of pyvista.core.filters.image_data.ImageDataFilters.contour_labels:146
msgid ""
"**simplify_output** : :ref:`bool <python:bltin-boolean-values>`, "
":obj:`optional`"
msgstr ""
"**simplify_output** : :ref:`bool <python:bltin-boolean-values>`, "
":obj:`optional`"

#: ../../../../../../../opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.13.14/x64/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pyvista/core/filters/image_data.pydocstring
#: of pyvista.core.filters.image_data.ImageDataFilters.contour_labels:147
msgid ""
"Simplify the ``'boundary_labels'`` array as a single-component 1D array. If "
"``False``, the returned ``'boundary_labels'`` array is a two-component 2D "
"array. This simplification is useful when only external boundaries are "
"generated and/or when visualizing internal boundaries. The simplification is"
" as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../../opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.13.14/x64/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pyvista/core/filters/image_data.pydocstring
#: of pyvista.core.filters.image_data.ImageDataFilters.contour_labels:153
msgid ""
"External boundaries are simplified by keeping the first component and "
"removing the second. Since external polygons may only share a boundary with "
"the background, the second component is always ``background_value`` and "
"therefore can be dropped without loss of information. The values of external"
" boundaries always match the foreground values of the input."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../../opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.13.14/x64/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pyvista/core/filters/image_data.pydocstring
#: of pyvista.core.filters.image_data.ImageDataFilters.contour_labels:159
msgid ""
"Internal boundaries are simplified by assigning them unique negative values "
"sequentially. E.g. the boundary label ``[1, 2]`` is replaced with ``-1``, "
"``[1, 3]`` is replaced with ``-2``, etc. The mapping to negative values is "
"not fixed, and can change depending on the input."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../../opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.13.14/x64/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pyvista/core/filters/image_data.pydocstring
#: of pyvista.core.filters.image_data.ImageDataFilters.contour_labels:164
msgid ""
"This simplification is particularly useful for unsigned integer labels (e.g."
" scalars with ``'uint8'`` dtype) since external boundaries will be positive "
"and internal boundaries will be negative in this case."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../../opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.13.14/x64/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pyvista/core/filters/image_data.pydocstring
#: of pyvista.core.filters.image_data.ImageDataFilters.contour_labels:168
msgid ""
"By default, the output is simplified when ``boundary_type`` is "
"``'external'`` or ``'strict_external'``, and is not simplified otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../../opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.13.14/x64/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pyvista/core/filters/image_data.pydocstring
#: of pyvista.core.filters.image_data.ImageDataFilters.contour_labels:171
msgid ""
"**smoothing** : :ref:`bool <python:bltin-boolean-values>`, default: "
":data:`python:True`"
msgstr ""
"**smoothing** : :ref:`bool <python:bltin-boolean-values>`, default: "
":data:`python:True`"

#: ../../../../../../../opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.13.14/x64/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pyvista/core/filters/image_data.pydocstring
#: of pyvista.core.filters.image_data.ImageDataFilters.contour_labels:172
msgid ""
"Smooth the generated surface using a constrained smoothing filter. Each "
"point in the surface is smoothed as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../../opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.13.14/x64/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pyvista/core/filters/image_data.pydocstring
#: of pyvista.core.filters.image_data.ImageDataFilters.contour_labels:175
msgid ""
"For a point ``pi`` connected to a list of points ``pj`` via an edge, ``pi`` "
"is moved towards the average position of ``pj`` multiplied by the "
"``smoothing_relaxation`` factor, and limited by the ``smoothing_distance`` "
"constraint. This process is repeated either until convergence occurs, or the"
" maximum number of ``smoothing_iterations`` is reached."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../../opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.13.14/x64/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pyvista/core/filters/image_data.pydocstring
#: of pyvista.core.filters.image_data.ImageDataFilters.contour_labels:181
msgid "**smoothing_iterations** : :class:`python:int`, default: 16"
msgstr ""

