#: ../../pyvista/doc/source/api/readers/index.rst:129
msgid "Custom Writers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/doc/source/api/readers/index.rst:131
msgid ""
"Third-party packages can register custom writers so that "
":meth:`pyvista.DataObject.save` handles additional file formats "
"automatically.  Registration mirrors :func:`pyvista.register_reader` and "
"supports programmatic calls, decorators, and Python entry points for zero-"
"config discovery at install time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../../opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.13.14/x64/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pyvista/core/utilities/writer_registry.pydocstring
#: of pyvista.core.utilities.writer_registry.register_writer:2
msgid "Register a custom writer for a file extension."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../../opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.13.14/x64/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pyvista/core/utilities/writer_registry.pydocstring
#: of pyvista.core.utilities.writer_registry.register_writer:14
msgid ""
"A callable with signature ``handler(dataset, path, **kwargs)`` that writes "
"*dataset* to *path*.  Any extra keyword arguments passed to "
":meth:`pyvista.DataObject.save` are forwarded to the handler as ``**kwargs``"
" — use them to expose format-specific options such as compression level, "
"thread count, or chunking.  Handlers that do not need per-call options can "
"omit ``**kwargs``; a call to :meth:`~pyvista.DataObject.save` that passes "
"extras to such a handler will raise :class:`TypeError` from Python itself.  "
"When ``handler`` is omitted the function acts as a decorator and returns the"
" decorated callable unchanged."
msgstr ""

